// ============================================================================
// ENTERPRISE POWER BI ANALYTICS PORTFOLIO — DAX MEASURE LIBRARY
// Section: 07 Profitability (Financial Performance & Profit Drivers)
// Author: Datta Sable (https://dattasable.com)
// Source: Datta_Sable_PowerBI_DAX_Visuals_Implementation_Handbook.xlsx & PRD Section 6.7
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Gross Profit
// Purpose: Explicit financial metric for gross operating profit.
// Business Definition: Total sales revenue less direct order product cost.
// Expected Data Type: Currency
// Formatting: $#,##0.00
// Required Tables: fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: fact_orders_2023[Sales_Amount_USD], fact_orders_2023[Cost_Amount_USD]
// Filter Context Behavior: Evaluated across any active dimension (Category, Segment, Geography, Date).
// Recommended Visuals: Waterfall Chart, KPI Card, Gauge.
// Validation Method: Reconciles to [Total Sales] ($12,840,570.00) - [Total Cost] ($10,529,660.00) = $2,310,910.00.
// Known Limitations: Represents gross order margin before corporate operating overhead.
// ============================================================================
Gross Profit = 
[Total Sales] - [Total Cost]

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Cost Ratio %
// Purpose: Evaluates cost proportion relative to gross sales.
// Business Definition: Percentage of total sales consumed by cost of goods sold.
// Expected Data Type: Percentage
// Formatting: 0.0%
// Required Tables: fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: fact_orders_2023[Cost_Amount_USD], fact_orders_2023[Sales_Amount_USD]
// Filter Context Behavior: Uses safe division against total filtered sales.
// Recommended Visuals: Gauge, KPI Card, Donut Chart.
// Validation Method: $10,529,660 / $12,840,570 = 82.003% (Cost Ratio + Profit Margin = 100.0%).
// Known Limitations: Single-year baseline.
// ============================================================================
Cost Ratio % = 
DIVIDE ( [Total Cost], [Total Sales], 0 )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Category Profit Share %
// Purpose: Calculate category contribution to overall company profit.
// Business Definition: Ratio of category profit to total filtered profit.
// Expected Data Type: Percentage
// Formatting: 0.0%
// Required Tables: dim_products, fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: dim_products[Product_Category], fact_orders_2023[Profit_Amount_USD]
// Filter Context Behavior: Evaluated dynamically over the active filter context, removing filters from Product_Category.
// Recommended Visuals: 100% Stacked Bar Chart, Treemap, Matrix.
// Validation Method: Sum of Category Profit Share % across all product categories equals 100.0%.
// Known Limitations: Dependent on dim_products category hierarchy.
// ============================================================================
Category Profit Share % = 
DIVIDE ( [Total Profit], CALCULATE ( [Total Profit], ALLSELECTED ( dim_products[Product_Category] ) ) )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Cumulative Profit YTD
// Purpose: Track year-to-date profit accumulation.
// Business Definition: Running total of operating profit from the beginning of the calendar year.
// Expected Data Type: Currency
// Formatting: $#,##0.00
// Required Tables: DimDate, fact_orders_2023
// Required Columns: DimDate[Date], fact_orders_2023[Profit_Amount_USD]
// Filter Context Behavior: Requires marked DimDate date table.
// Recommended Visuals: Area Chart, Line Chart.
// Validation Method: December 31 cumulative profit equals $2,310,910.00.
// Known Limitations: Dependent on active calendar relationship.
// ============================================================================
Cumulative Profit YTD = 
TOTALYTD ( [Total Profit], DimDate[Date] )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Profit PY
// Purpose: Calculate prior year operating profit for variance comparisons.
// Business Definition: Operating profit for the corresponding calendar period in the prior year.
// Expected Data Type: Currency
// Formatting: $#,##0.00
// Required Tables: DimDate, fact_orders_2023
// Filter Context Behavior: Evaluated via SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR over DimDate[Date].
// Recommended Visuals: Multi-row Card, Clustered Column Chart with target lines.
// Validation Method: Requires 2022 historical transactional records; evaluates to BLANK() in single-year 2023 dataset.
// Known Limitations: In 2023 single-year baseline, prior period is blank.
// ============================================================================
Profit PY = 
CALCULATE ( [Total Profit], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR ( DimDate[Date] ) )

// ============================================================================
// Measure Name: Profit YoY %
// Purpose: Measure year-over-year percentage change in operating profit.
// Business Definition: Percentage growth or decline in profit compared to the same prior-year period.
// Expected Data Type: Percentage
// Formatting: 0.0%
// Required Tables: DimDate, fact_orders_2023
// Filter Context Behavior: Safe division between profit delta and prior-year profit.
// Recommended Visuals: KPI visual with indicator colors, Variance Waterfall.
// Validation Method: Returns BLANK() when [Profit PY] is not populated.
// Known Limitations: Requires two or more full years of history.
// ============================================================================
Profit YoY % = 
DIVIDE ( [Total Profit] - [Profit PY], [Profit PY] )
